%I A401046 #38 Oct 26 2026 09:53:52
%S A401046 16,100,12100,48400,62500,102400,168100,302500,409600,547600,774400,
%T A401046 940900,1416100,1612900,1876900,3610000,3841600,3880900,4120900,
%U A401046 4243600,4368100,6300100,7398400,13542400,14822500,15288100,16810000,17305600,20340100,23232400,24403600
%N A401046 Sexy squares: squares that are the sum of two primes differing by 6.
%C A401046 A number a(n) belongs to this sequence if a(n) = k^2 = p + q, where k is integer, p and q are prime numbers and q = p + 6.
%C A401046 Equivalently, writing k = 2m, the two primes must be p = 2m^2 - 3 and q = 2m^2 + 3. Thus the sequence consists of the values 4m^2 for which both 2m^2 - 3 and 2m^2 + 3 are prime.
%C A401046 All terms are divisible by 100, except of the initial term 16 = 5 + 11 = 4^2.
%C A401046 No sexy square is divisible by 3, which implies that sexy squares are disjoint from squares which are sums of twin primes, as these are always divisible by 3. Moreover sexy squares cannot be sums of cousin primes, as cousin primes never add up to squares.
%C A401046 It is not known whether this sequence is infinite. However, assuming the Bateman-Horn conjecture, infinitude would follow.
%H A401046 Peer Stelldinger, <a href="/A401046/b401046.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401046 Peer Stelldinger, <a href="/A401046/a401046.py.txt">Python script to compute larger values of the sequence</a>
%F A401046 a(n) = 2 * A086776(n) + 6. - _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 15 2026
%F A401046 a(n) = A401045(n)^2. - _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 26 2026
%e A401046 a(1) = 16 = 4^2 = 5 + 11, where 5 and 11 are prime.
%e A401046 a(2) = 100 = 10^2 = 47 + 53, where 47 and 53 are prime.
%e A401046 a(3) = 12100 = 110^2 = 6047 + 6053, where 6047 and 6053 are prime.
%t A401046 Join[{16}, Select[Range[10, 5000, 10]^2, PrimeQ[#] && PrimeQ[# + 6] & [#/2 - 3] &]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 26 2026 *)
%o A401046 (PARI) for(m = 2, 5000, {my(p = 2*m^2 - 3); if(isprime(p) && isprime(p + 6), print1(4*m^2,", "););})
%Y A401046 Intersection of A000290 and A104010.
%Y A401046 Cf. A023201, A046117, A401045, A086776, A037072.
%K A401046 nonn,new
%O A401046 1,1
%A A401046 Anna Kathrin Holtwiesche and _Peer Stelldinger_, Oct 14 2026
